   139.01 DUTIES OF CHIEF.
   The Chief of Police shall perform all duties and services usually performed
by such officers under the laws of the State.
(Ord. 91. Passed 10-11-43. )
   139.02 LIEUTENANT.
   There is hereby established the position of Lieutenant, which position shall
be filled by appointment by the Mayor with the approval of Council, which
appointee shall continue in office until removed therefrom for the causes and
under the powers and procedures provided by law. The position of Lieutenant
shall be in the classified civil service of the City, irrespective of whether
or not the person occupying that position is deemed to be the assistant
department head of the Police Department.
(Ord. 1997-175. Passed 9-8-97.)
   139.03 SERGEANT.
   There shall be five positions of Sergeant within the Division of Police to
be filled by appointment by the Mayor with the approval of Council. Each
appointee shall continue in office until removed therefrom for the causes and
under the powers and procedures provided by law. (Ord. 1986-11. Passed 1-27-
86.)
   139.04 CLASSES OF PATROLMEN.
   There is hereby created two classes of patrolmen to be known as Class A and
Class B.
(Ord. 1957-217. Passed 3-18-57.)
   139.05 PART-TIME PATROLMEN.
   Each part-time patrolman shall be under the direction and supervision of the
Chief of Police and shall carry out the duties and orders and shall work such
hours as set forth by the Chief of Police.
(Ord. 1957-225. Passed 8-19-57. )
   139.051 DETECTIVES.
   The Chief of Police may assign from time to time and at his discretion a
member or members of the police force to serve as detectives. Except for the
uniform allowance set forth in Section
161.18, persons so assigned shall not receive additional compensation and no
special testing shall be required for the assignment.
(Ord. 1981-73. Passed 9-28-81.)
   139.06 UNIFORM ALLOWANCES.
   In addition to any other compensation paid to the members of the Division of
Police, each member shall receive an annual uniform allowance, as provided in
Section
161.18.
   Uniform allowance shall be payable on presentation of invoices for the
purchase of uniform clothing or dry-cleaning thereof to the Finance Director
who shall dispense the same monthly up to the maximum amounts allowed. In
addition, any piece of uniform damaged in the line of duty will be replaced by
the City upon approval of the Public Safety Director or Mayor.
(Ord. 1973-824. Passed 6-11-73.)
   139.07 AGE LIMIT FOR APPOINTMENT.
   No person shall be eligible to receive an original full-time appointment to
the Police Department unless he or she is twenty-one years of age or older.
(Ord. 1991-25. Passed 2-27-91.)
