   141.01 DIVISION OF FIRE CREATED.
   There is hereby created a Division of Fire which shall at all times be under
the control and direction of the Safety Director and Council.
(Ord. 1989-26. Passed 5-22-89.)
   141.02 COMPOSITION OF DIVISION OF FIRE.
   The Division of Fire shall have a staff consisting of a Chief, an Assistant
Chief, three Captains, three Lieutenants and a maximum number of forty
firefighters. The make-up of which shall include both full-time and part-time
positions. All members shall be appointed by the Mayor, subject to the
provisions hereinafter made and with the advice and consent of Council, and
shall serve until removed for good cause shown in accordance with Ohio R.C.
733.35 to 733.39 inclusive. Full-time personnel shall be appointed pursuant to
the provisions of Section
181.05.
   The personnel of the Division of Fire as herein established, shall be paid
at the rate set forth in the compensation schedules of Chapter
161 or by contract with the City.
(Ord. 2002-206. Passed 11-15-02.)
   141.03 UNIFORM ALLOWANCE.
   In addition to any compensation paid to the personnel of the Division of
Fire, each member shall receive a uniform allowance as provided in Chapter
161 or by contract with the City.
(Ord. 1989-26. Passed 5-22-89.)
   141.04 PARAMEDIC CERTIFICATION.
   All personnel appointed to the Full-Time Firefighter/Paramedic position
shall be a certified Paramedic prior to appointment and shall maintain their
Paramedic status as such during their employment with the City.
(Ord. 1989-26. Passed 5-22-89.)
   141.05 VACANCIES, PROMOTIONS AND DEMOTIONS IN THE DIVISION OF FIRE.
   (a)   Whenever a vacancy occurs in the part-time personnel of the Division
of Fire, the Chief, after consultation with the officers, shall recommend to
the Mayor the name or names of persons deeded worthy of appointment to such
vacancy.
   (b)   All promotions and demotions of part-time personnel in the Division of
Fire shall be made by the Mayor, with the advice of the Fire Chief and
Officers, and the advice and consent of Council.
(Ord. 1989-26. Passed 5-22-89; Ord. 2002-206. Passed 11-15-02.)
   (c)   All vacancies, promotions, demotions of full-time personnel within the
Division of Fire shall be made pursuant to the Ohio Revised Code. Entry level
vacancies shall be filled from the top seven on the eligibility list, pursuant
to the provisions of Section
181.05 .
(Ord. 2007-062. Passed 5-14-07.)
   141.06 ABSENCE OF CHIEF.
   During the absence, inability or refusal of the Fire Chief to act, his
duties shall revolve upon the next ranking office in charge.
(Ord. 1989-26. Passed 5-22-89; Ord. 2002-206. Passed 11-15-02.)
   141.07 USE OF PART-TIME TO FILL IN FOR FULL-TIME.
   The Chief of the Division of Fire may employ part-time firefighters to fill
in for any of the full-time personnel, in the case of sickness, days off or
vacations.
(Ord. 1989-26. Passed 5-22-89; Ord. 2002-206. Passed 11-15-02.)
   141.08 MEETING AND DRILLS.
   It is the duty of each member of the Division of Fire to attend all meetings
and drills. Regular meeting shall be held twice each month for drill and
instruction. Special meetings may be called as often as deemed necessary by the
Fire Chief, after giving one week's written notice to each member of the
Division of Fire.
(Ord. 1989-26. Passed 5-22-89; Ord. 2002-206. Passed 11-15-02.)
   141.09 AGE LIMIT FOR APPOINTMENT.
   (a)    In accordance with Ohio R.C. 124.42, the Mayor may appoint any
competent person who is not over thirty-six years of age to a full-time
position in the Division of Fire.
   (b)    The Mayor may appoint any person not over forty years of age to a
full-time position in the Division of Fire providing he has prior service and
qualifies as being a member of the Ohio Police and Firemen's Disability and
Pension Fund and that such service and membership has continued for not less
than four years prior to appointment.
   (c)    The Mayor may appoint any competent person not over fifty years of
age to a part-time position in the Division of Fire.
(Ord. 1989-26. Passed 5-22-89; Ord. 2002-206. Passed 11-15-02.)
