CHAPTER 152
Division of Wastewater Treatment
152.01    Establishment.
152.02    Personnel.
   152.01 ESTABLISHMENT.
   There is hereby established a Division of Wastewater Treatment of the
Department of Public Services to be responsible for the operation and general
maintenance of a wastewater treatment and disposal system utilizing wastewater
lift stations, pressure mains and biological treatment of the City’s wastewater
treatment plants and facilities.
(Ord. 2007-070. Passed 4-23-07.)
   152.02 PERSONNEL.
   The Division shall consist of a Wastewater Facilities Manager who shall
report to the Director of the Department of Public Services and such other
employees as shall be deemed necessary including, but not limited to, an
Assistant Wastewater Facilities Manager, Wastewater Laboratory Operator and
Wastewater Maintenance Operator.
(Ord. 2007-070. Passed 4-23-07.)
CHAPTER 153
Division of Parks and Recreation
153.01   Establishment.
153.02   Director.
153.03   Jurisdiction of division.
153.04   Recreation Advisory Committee.
153.05    Use and charges for City’s athletic facilities.
CROSS REFERENCES
      Compensation - see CHTR. Sec.
3.09
      Council authority to create Department - see CHTR. Sec.
3.15
      Director of Public Service, responsibility for parks - see CHTR. Sec.
9.01
      Parks and recreation - see CHTR. Sec.
10.01
      Sunny Lake fees and charges - see ADM.
111.01(c)
   153.01 ESTABLISHMENT.
   There is hereby established a Division of Parks and Recreation of the
Department of Public Service consisting of a Parks and Recreation Division
Director and such other employees as may be authorized by ordinance of Council.
(Ord. 2016-017. Passed 3-28-16.)
   153.02 DIRECTOR.
   The Director of the Division of Parks and Recreation shall be the head of
the Division of Parks and Recreation and shall be appointed by, and report to,
the Mayor.
(Ord. 2016-017. Passed 3-28-16.)
   153.03 JURISDICTION OF DIVISION.
   The Division of Parks and Recreation shall be responsible for the
maintenance of public parks, recreation areas and bike paths within the City.
The Division shall also be responsible for establishing and administering
recreation programs, sports programs, senior programs, community education and
special events. (Ord. 2016-017. Passed 3-18-16.)
   153.04 RECREATION ADVISORY COMMITTEE.
   (a)   Purpose. The purpose of the Recreation Advisory Committee is to
discuss and submit ideas for recreation activities within the City and
generally assist in creating an ongoing line of communication between the City
and its citizens concerning recreation programs.
   (b)    Establishment and Membership. There is hereby established a
Recreation Advisory Committee to consist of seven members who shall advise the
Director with respect to matters set forth herein. Six members shall be
appointed by the Mayor. The committee will be as follows:
      (1)   One member of Council, appointed by Council.
      (2)   Three residents of the City, not holding other public office within
the City, appointed by the Mayor, to serve a term ending midnight, December 31,
2012. Thereafter, the term shall be for two years. Successive terms shall be
permitted.
      (3)   Three residents of the City, not holding public office within the
City, appointed by the Mayor, to serve a term ending midnight, December 31,
2013. Thereafter, the terms shall be for two years. Successive terms shall be
permitted.
   To the extent practical, the City shall endeavor to insure representation
from the various youth athletic associations and senior citizens.
   (c)    Meetings and Officers. The committee shall meet quarterly or as
needed. At its first meeting of each year a chairman and vice-chairman shall be
elected. A majority of the members shall constitute a quorum and any actions of
the committee may be taken by a majority of the members present at the meeting
at which the action is taken. The committee shall keep minutes of its meetings
and file them with the Clerk of Council. A special meeting may be called by the
chairman, or in his/her absence, the vice-chairman or by any two of the
committee members. The committee may adopt its own rules.
   (d)    Jurisdiction. The committee shall advise the Director regarding
guidelines for establishing and administering the City's recreation, sports,
senior programs, community education and special events. (Ord. 2016-017. Passed
3-28-16.)
   153.05 USE AND CHARGES FOR CITY’S ATHLETIC FACILITIES.
   (a)    The City's athletic facilities shall not be made available for use by
any sports teams or associations except those actually sponsored and operated
by the division of Parks and Recreation and/or by the Aurora City Schools
without the prior written consent of the Director of Parks and Recreation and
the prior agreement on the part of such interested teams or associations to
hold the City harmless from any and all liabilities arising in connection with
such usage and to compensate the City as set forth hereafter.
   (b)    Approval of the use of such facilities shall be in the sole
discretion of the Director.
   (c)    There is hereby imposed an athletic facilities usage fee of ten
dollars ($10.00) per participant per season for such approved sports teams or
associations to use the City's athletic facilities to compensate the city for
all reasonable additional costs and expenses incurred by the City as a result
of such activities. Each team or association shall be responsible for reporting
the total number of participants for each activity for each season and for
submitting the per participant fee to the Director.
   (d)    The City shall be responsible to prepare the respective facility for
game use.
   (e)    The athletic facilities usage fee may be adjusted from time to time
by Council upon the recommendation of the Recreation Advisory Committee.
(Ord. 2016-017. Passed 3-28-16.)
CHAPTER 154
Department of Recreation
(EDITOR’S NOTE: Former Chapter
154, was repealed by Ordinance 2007-210.)
CHAPTER 155
Division of Engineering, Utilities and Inspection
155.01    Establishment.
155.02    Director.
155.03    Jurisdiction of the Division.
155.04    Duties generally.
CROSS REFERENCES
      Compensation - see CHTR. §
3.09 
      Subdivision procedures - see P. & Z. Ch.
1105
      Design standards for subdivisions - see P. & Z. Ch.
1109
      Driveway grade determination - see BLDG.
1323.01(c)
   155.01 ESTABLISHMENT.
   There is hereby established a Division of Engineering, Utilities and
Inspection of the Department of Public Services consisting of a Director of
Engineering, Utilities and Inspection and such other employees as may be
authorized by ordinance of Council.
(Ord. 2016-029. Passed 5-5-16.)
   155.02 DIRECTOR.
   The Director shall be the head of the Division of Engineering, Utilities and
Inspection of the Department of Public Services and shall be appointed by the
Mayor. The Director, or in the absence of a Director, such other professional
engineers employed, or retained by the City, shall report to the Director of
Public Services. As used elsewhere in these codified ordinances, references to
the Director shall be deemed to include, as applicable and appropriate, other
professional engineers employed by the City or retained by the City as
independent contractors.
(Ord. 2016-029. Passed 5-5-16.)
   155.03 JURISDICTION OF THE DIVISION.
   (a)   The Division of Engineering, Utilities and Inspection shall be
responsible for providing professional civil engineering work in at an
administrative, supervisory and technical level, coordinating and directing all
activities regarding engineering, utilities and inspection including the
Geographic Information System (GIS) function. Utilities include Sanitary Sewer,
Waste Water Treatment Plants, City Water Services and Septic Systems.
   
   (b)   The Division shall direct and participate with department engineers
and contract consultants in the investigation, development, design and
construction of a variety of public engineering projects. The Division shall
control field work and on site inspections; review reports and authorize
changes to projects within the scope of the contract; coordinate public works
with city departments and state and federal agencies and utility companies;
plan and implement additions, modifications, and/or deletions relative to
water, wastewater, storm and septic systems, in addition to other public
utilities including, but not limited to, telephone, cable, gas and electric;
review proposed subdivisions of land, including residential, commercial and
industrial site plans for conformity to City standards, City Ordinances and
good engineering practice; and inform the Planning Commission accordingly.
(Ord. 2016-029. Passed 5-5-16.)
   155.04 DUTIES GENERALLY.
   The Director shall, from time to time, promulgate, amend, adopt and publish
guidelines for use in enforcing and administering and divisional duties.
(Ord. 2016-029. Passed 5-5-16.)
