      Board of Zoning Appeals - see P. & Z.
1137.03
   173.01 ESTABLISHMENT.
   There is hereby established in the City the Board of Building Code Appeals
(hereafter “the Board”).
(Ord. 2005-009. Passed 2-28-05.)
   173.02 APPOINTMENT OF MEMBERS.
   (a)   The Board shall consist of five electors of the municipality qualified
by experience and training to pass upon matters pertaining to the current
residential building code of the City of Aurora (hereafter “the Code”).
   (b)   The five members shall each be appointed by the Mayor and confirmed by
Council for a period of four (4) years, ending on December 31 of the fourth
year. Every two (2) years, the Mayor shall appoint, or reappoint, persons to
serve in either two (2) or three (3) of the member positions so that the period
of service for new members shall always overlap the period of service of other
members.
   (c)   In the event of death or resignation of a member, the Mayor, with the
approval of Council, shall make the appointment for the duration of the
unexpired portion of the term of the member.
(Ord. 2005-009. Passed 2-28-05.)
   173.03 QUORUM.
   Three members of the Board shall constitute a quorum. In varying the
application of any provision of the Code, affirmative votes of three members
shall be required.
(Ord. 2005-009. Passed 2-28-05.)
   173.04 DISQUALIFICATION.
   No member of the Board shall vote on any matter in which he or she has a
financial or personal interest, in accordance with the Charter and Codified
Ordinances of the City of Aurora and applicable State of Ohio and federal laws.
(Ord. 2005-009. Passed 2-28-05.)
   173.05 COMPENSATION.
   The members of the Board shall serve without compensation.
(Ord. 2005-009. Passed 2-28-05.)
   173.06 SCOPE OF AUTHORITY.
    The Board shall have the authority to:
   (a)   Affirm, reverse or modify, in whole or in part, any decision of the
building official interpreting the provisions of the Code;
   (b)   Vary the application of any provision of the Code to any particular
case when, in its collective opinion, enforcement thereof would do manifest
injustice or would be contrary to the spirit and purpose of the Code or the
public interest;
   (c)    Determine if any material or method of construction may be used, even
if not specifically authorized by the Code or the public interest; and
   (d)    Determine whether any proposed rule of the building official
supplements or aids in the interpretation of the requirements of the Code and
is consistent with it, and to amend, modify, or nullify any such proposed rule.
      (Ord. 2005-009. Passed 2-28-05.)
   173.07 MEETINGS AND RECORDS.
   Meetings of the Board shall be held at the call of the chairman and at such
other times as the Board may determine. All hearings before the board shall be
open to the public. The Board shall keep minutes of its proceedings, showing
the vote of each member upon every question, or if absent or failing to vote,
indicating such facts, and shall also keep records of its other official
actions. Such minutes and such records shall be public records.
(Ord. 2005-009. Passed 2-28-05.)
   173.08 PROCEDURES.
   The Board shall establish rules and regulations for its own procedures.
(Ord. 2005-009. Passed 2-28-05.)
   173.09 APPEAL TO BOARD.
   (a)   Any person, any municipal officer or official, or any public body
aggrieved by the action of the Building Official may take an appeal to the
Board.
   (b)   The Building Official, any municipal officer or official, any public
body, or any member of the Board may request a hearing by the Board on any
subject over which the Board has jurisdiction or power, or may request the
Board to review or interpret any provision of the Code.
(Ord. 2005-009. Passed 2-28-05.)
   173.10 TIME, FEE AND NOTICE OF APPEAL.
   An appeal from any decision of the Building Official may be taken within
thirty days of that decision by paying the required fee of seventy-five dollars
($75.00) and filing a notice of appeal on the form provided by the Building
Department. In the event the Board finds it necessary to obtain any legal,
engineering or other expert testimony, the appellant shall be responsible for
any costs associated therewith. The filing of an appeal shall stay any further
action of the Building Official until such appeal is resolved.
(Ord. 2005-009. Passed 2-28-05.)
   173.11 ACTION ON APPEALS, HEARING, AND REVIEWS.
   (a)    Notice. The Board shall hold a public hearing on each appeal and
shall give such notice to the Building Official and other interested parties as
the Board shall direct and shall give such notice to the public by posting,
publication or otherwise as the Board shall deem appropriate. At the hearing,
any party may appear in person, or by his agent or attorney.
   (b)    Evidence and inspection. In passing upon appeals, the Board may
require submission of evidence or proof to substantiate claims, and may require
such additional data and tests which, in the opinion of the Board, are needed
for adequate consideration of the appeal. Any member of the Board or any person
authorized by the Board may at any time enter, inspect and examine any plans,
building or structure for the purpose of carrying out the duties of the Board.
(Ord. 2005-009. Passed 2-28-05.)
   173.12 DECISIONS GENERAL.
   The Board shall in every case reach a decision without unreasonable or
unnecessary delay. Every decision of the Board shall be in writing and shall
indicate the vote upon the decision. Every decision shall be promptly filed
with the Building Department and shall be open to public inspection. A
certified copy shall be sent by mail or otherwise to the appellant.
(Ord. 2005-009. Passed 2-28-05.)
   173.13 VARIATIONS AND MODIFICATIONS.
   The Board, after public hearing, may vary the application of any provision
of the Code to any particular case when, in its opinion, enforcement thereof
would do manifest injustice, would be contrary to the spirit and purpose of the
Code or public interest, or when, in its opinion, the interpretation of the
Building Official should be modified or reversed. A decision of the Board to
vary the application of any provision of the Code or to modify an order of the
Building Official shall specify in what manner such variation or modification
is made, the conditions upon which it is made, and the reasons therefore.
(Ord. 2005-009. Passed 2-28-05.)
   173.14 BUILDING OFFICIAL TO TAKE ACTION.
   If a decision of the Board reverses or modifies a refusal, order or
disallowance of the Building Official or varies the application of any
provision of the Code, the Building Official shall take action immediately in
accordance with such decision.
(Ord. 2005-009. Passed 2-28-05.)
